PERMISSION DATABASE MODEL

Implement the shared permission model using existing structures where possible.

The permission model must support these layers:

Level 0:
Explicit user permission override.

* user
* resource/scope
* permission
* allow/deny

Level 1:
System role.
Examples:

* Super Admin
* Admin
* Viewer

Level 2:
Application role.
An application-specific role that applies only to one application.

Level 3:
Record/entity-level access.
This should integrate with the existing contributor/ownership model and hierarchy inheritance rather than creating a second contributor system.

Knowledge Base permissions must be capable of expressing:

* Knowledge Base scope
* Hierarchy Node scope
* Workflow scope
* Content Type scope

